> There's a nice piece of software I love deeply with all my heart - OpenSnitch application firewall (https://github.com/evilsocket/opensnitch). It warns you and allows to block whatever network calls your apps are making. But the frontend is a gui thing, so if you're running opencode remotely on some headless server, it's not an option.

@kha84 You can install the OpenSnitch traffic monitoring daemon on a the headless server, and the GUI on your local machine:

https://github.com/evilsocket/opensnitch/wiki/Nodes

[Workaround/Fix] 

add vision support manually

{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "disabled_providers": [],
  "provider": {
    "janai": {
      "name": "janai",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://127.0.0.1:3872/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "Qwopus3.6-27B-v2-Q8_0.gguf": {
          "name": "Qwopus3.6-27B-v2-Q8_0",
          "limit": {
            "context": 250000,
            "output": 8192
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "lmstudio_local": {
      "name": "lmstudio_local",
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "http://192.168.1.130:1234/v1"
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.6-27b": {
          "name": "qwen3.6-27b",
          "attachment": true,
          "modalities": {
            "input": [
              "text",
              "image"
            ],
            "output": [
              "text"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}




Comment:

Root Cause: Opencode caches the model's capabilities on startup. If you update opencode.json to enable a vision-capable model (or change model settings), the vision pipeline isn't activated until the process is restarted.

Workaround: After updating ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, restart opencode completely:

# Kill existing process
taskkill /F /IM opencode.exe  # Windows
# or pkill opencode           # Linux/Mac

# Restart
opencode

Proposed Fix:

Hot-reload config: Detect changes to opencode.json and reload model capabilities without requiring a restart.
Add GUI for mmprog file or detect automatically.

Auto-detect vision: Check for mmproj files in the model directory on startup and automatically enable the vision pipeline, so users don't need to manually configure it.
Better error message: Instead of "this model does not support image input", show "this model has vision capabilities but vision is not enabled. Try restarting opencode after updating your config."
